WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.055
<v Examiner>Two marks.

2
00:00:02.055 --> 00:00:06.117
<v Examiner>Why does Joan call them antimicrobials rather than antibiotics?

3
00:00:06.117 --> 00:00:10.114
<v Examiner>And give one nursing consideration before giving a penicillin.

4
00:00:10.564 --> 00:00:15.147
Antimicrobial is the big family: anything that acts on microbes.

5
00:00:15.147 --> 00:00:20.160
Antibiotics act on bacteria, but the family also includes antifungals,

6
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.309
antivirals and antiparasitics.

7
00:00:22.309 --> 00:00:25.102
So antibiotics are just one sub-family.

8
00:00:25.102 --> 00:00:29.327
The penicillins are antibiotics: their names end in cillin,

9
00:00:29.327 --> 00:00:31.905
like amoxicillin and flucloxacillin,

10
00:00:31.905 --> 00:00:36.130
and they kill bacteria by damaging the bacterial cell wall.

11
00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:39.635
Before giving one: ask about allergy, every time.

12
00:00:39.635 --> 00:00:44.062
Of all the drug classes, antibiotics cause the most allergic reactions,

13
00:00:44.062 --> 00:00:46.805
and penicillin allergy can mean anaphylaxis.

14
00:00:46.805 --> 00:00:50.796
After giving it, especially a first dose, watch for rash, hives,

15
00:00:50.796 --> 00:00:52.666
swelling or breathing trouble.

16
00:00:52.666 --> 00:00:55.721
And teach the patient to finish the whole course,

17
00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:59.151
because stopping early helps bacteria become resistant.

18
00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:05.888
Antimicrobials are the whole family: antibiotics, antifungals, antivirals, antiparasitics.

19
00:01:05.888 --> 00:01:11.476
Penicillins end in cillin, like amoxicillin, and damage the bacterial cell wall.

20
00:01:11.476 --> 00:01:17.414
Ask about allergy before every first dose; antibiotics cause the most drug allergies.

21
00:01:17.414 --> 00:01:18.951
Watch for anaphylaxis.

22
00:01:18.951 --> 00:01:20.209
Finish the course.
